Mandatory rules:

- Never invent statistics, dates, routes, station names or technical specifications.
- Prefer official government and operator sources.
- Clearly distinguish operational, partially operational, under-construction, approved, proposed and cancelled projects.
- Attach sources to important factual claims.
- Include reporting dates for statistics.
- Maintain historical snapshots.
- Clearly mark unavailable or unverified information.
- Do not treat estimates as confirmed figures.
- Record the date when information was last verified.

